WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.940 --> 00:00:03.390
- [Narrator] If you've
got shopping for screws

00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:05.000
at Home Depot or Lowe's,

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:07.860
chances are they came
from Henry Chen's factory.

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:09.473
- We have been producing this screw

00:00:09.473 --> 00:00:13.890
for about approximately 10 years
out of our China operation.

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:17.040
- [Narrator] But now, these
screws are made in Taiwan.

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.060
American demand for goods from the island,

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:21.350
whether it's hardware, toys, or furniture,

00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:23.370
has grown a lot in recent years.

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:26.440
Taiwan also controls more
than 90% of the world's supply

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:28.210
of the most advanced chips,

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:31.700
which end up in almost everything
from electronics to cars.

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:36.630
In 2021, these exports to the
U.S. had a record $72 billion,

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:39.790
up about 70% since 2017.

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:42.390
This booming trade between
the U.S. and Taiwan comes

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:44.370
as both governments have also strengthened

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:46.250
their military relationship.

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:48.629
And this closeness has angered Beijing.

00:00:48.629 --> 00:00:50.416
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:50.416 --> 00:00:52.530
- Companies can get caught in the middle

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:54.840
of different governments,

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:57.713
competing with each other
for power and influence.

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:00.150
- [Narrator] So, we visited this factory

00:01:00.150 --> 00:01:02.060
to see how geopolitical tensions

00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:04.753
have made operating a
business in Taiwan trickier.

00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:12.150
- So, these screws,

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:16.040
these are typically
used on top of roofing,

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:17.520
they're roofing screws.

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:20.580
- [Narrator] Henry Chen,
overseas operations at JC Grand,

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.660
one of the leading Taiwanese manufacturers

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:25.913
of construction fasteners,
since the late 1970s.

00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:28.960
Back then, Taiwan was one of the world's

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:32.453
biggest manufacturing hubs
alongside Japan and South Korea.

00:01:33.890 --> 00:01:36.730
In the 1980s, China started
opening up its economy

00:01:36.730 --> 00:01:38.840
to the world, including Taiwan.

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:41.300
Which has been separately
governed since 1949,

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:43.690
when the Nationalist
Party, fled the mainland

00:01:43.690 --> 00:01:47.250
after being defeated by communist
forces. (people cheering)

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:49.100
So, in hope of reunification,

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:52.030
Beijing welcomed Taiwanese
companies to the mainland,

00:01:52.030 --> 00:01:53.370
hoping to cool tensions

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:56.350
and make China the world's
factory that it is today.

00:01:56.350 --> 00:01:59.260
- You see in China there's
lower commodity and labor cost.

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:02.370
The cost of China versus Taiwan

00:02:02.370 --> 00:02:05.030
for us, just purely on a production level,

00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:07.760
it was about five to 10% cheaper.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:10.760
- JC Grand expanded to China in 2001,

00:02:10.760 --> 00:02:12.730
and eventually close
to half of its products

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:13.810
were made there,

00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:14.970
but that started to change

00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:17.350
at the height of the U.S.-China Trade War.

00:02:17.350 --> 00:02:20.200
- The United States has
just announced tariffs

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:24.990
on another $200 billion
in Chinese made goods.

00:02:24.990 --> 00:02:25.970
- With the tariff,

00:02:25.970 --> 00:02:29.060
it made our China
operation so much harder.

00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:31.100
- [Narrator] In 2018,
the Trump Administration

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:34.680
imposed a hefty 25% levy
on many Chinese products,

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:35.943
like Chen's 10 screws.

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:39.240
He said it was one of the
first times he realized

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:40.840
how U.S.-China tensions,

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:43.840
could have an immediate
financial impact on the business.

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:45.860
So, the company had to make a decision,

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:50.370
stay in China and raise
prices or move somewhere else.

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:55.370
- Taiwan has the benefit of
just having so much know-how

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:58.180
that's being kept here
for the past 40 years.

00:02:58.180 --> 00:03:03.180
So, it was primarily a
Taiwan-China decision for us.

00:03:03.460 --> 00:03:05.920
This is one of the examples of the items

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:08.860
that we shift the production
from China to Taiwan.

00:03:08.860 --> 00:03:10.870
- [Narrator] Since the
tarrifs were first introduced,

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:12.610
Chen's company isn't the only one

00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:15.310
that has returned some
production back home.

00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:19.160
Taipei has convinced more than
250 companies to relocate,

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:22.210
by offering financial
incentives and resources.

00:03:22.210 --> 00:03:24.570
And this surge in manufacturing capacity

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:27.790
has helped U.S. trade
with the island boom.

00:03:27.790 --> 00:03:31.610
(speaking in foreign language)

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:33.190
- [Narrator] Shortly after taking office,

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:34.930
President Biden sent a delegation

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:36.820
to meet with the Taiwanese leader.

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:39.130
Who's been actively
seeking a free trade deal,

00:03:39.130 --> 00:03:42.590
similar to ones the U.S.
has with Canada and Mexico.

00:03:42.590 --> 00:03:44.610
And the relationship
isn't just about commerce,

00:03:44.610 --> 00:03:46.120
but also security.

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:47.700
For instance, the U.S. has sent

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:50.270
special forces troops
and Marines to Taiwan,

00:03:50.270 --> 00:03:51.749
to train soldiers.

00:03:51.749 --> 00:03:53.580
- So, you're saying that the United States

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:56.570
would come to Taiwan's
defense if China attacked.

00:03:56.570 --> 00:03:58.010
- Yes, we have a commitment.

00:03:58.010 --> 00:03:59.060
- [Narrator] Commitments like this,

00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:00.840
though later hedged by the White House,

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.950
have been met with protests from Beijing,

00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:05.747
which has told the U.S.
to stop interfering.

00:04:05.747 --> 00:04:09.664
(speaking in foreign language)

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:16.000
Beijing has also sent warnings to Taipei,

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:17.510
by conducting military drills

00:04:17.510 --> 00:04:19.550
about 100 miles from its shores,

00:04:19.550 --> 00:04:23.110
while sending spy planes
and bombers near the island.

00:04:23.110 --> 00:04:25.770
So, as Taiwan builds
stronger ties with the U.S.,

00:04:25.770 --> 00:04:27.600
it's been moving away from China,

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:31.160
and this dynamic could pull
each of them into a conflict.

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:36.160
- The Taiwan issue has been
a challenge for a long time.

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:38.520
- [Narrator] Scott Kennedy, is with the

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:40.570
Bipartisan Foreign Policy think tank,

00:04:40.570 --> 00:04:43.490
the Center for Strategic
and International Studies.

00:04:43.490 --> 00:04:47.400
He's been watching U.S.-China
relations for over 30 years.

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:48.810
- In the last several years,

00:04:48.810 --> 00:04:52.580
Chinese Policy has grown
even more antagonistic.

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:55.220
There's been concern about whether or not

00:04:55.220 --> 00:04:57.650
China may be preparing to use force

00:04:57.650 --> 00:04:59.730
and has given up on its goal

00:04:59.730 --> 00:05:04.730
of peacefully resolving the
political questions with Taiwan.

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:05.750
- [Narrator] While security experts say

00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:07.730
the chances of a war are low,

00:05:07.730 --> 00:05:10.660
any missteps by the U.S.,China or Taiwan,

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:12.880
could leave companies
that operate on the island

00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:15.700
or the mainland, in a vulnerable position.

00:05:15.700 --> 00:05:18.760
- The more assortive China has become,

00:05:18.760 --> 00:05:21.270
it's a challenge for every company

00:05:21.270 --> 00:05:22.770
to try and thread that needle.

00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:26.200
- [Narrator] For JC Gran,
threading the needle means

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:28.460
running factories in China and Taiwan,

00:05:28.460 --> 00:05:30.160
with the wait and see about.

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:33.730
- We see our China operation
as being very steady

00:05:33.730 --> 00:05:34.680
for the time being,

00:05:35.670 --> 00:05:39.320
but there probably won't
be too many opportunities

00:05:39.320 --> 00:05:41.150
to make major investments,

00:05:41.150 --> 00:05:43.560
partially, because of the uncertainties

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:46.050
with the U.S.-China relations.

00:05:46.050 --> 00:05:47.170
- [Narrator] The company is also weighing

00:05:47.170 --> 00:05:49.510
whether to shift more
production to Taiwan,

00:05:49.510 --> 00:05:51.720
but that decision comes
with other challenges,

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:54.030
given the small islands increasing focus

00:05:54.030 --> 00:05:56.040
on manufacturing chips.

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:58.930
- Labor cost is gonna be
an issue going forward.

00:05:58.930 --> 00:06:00.810
And that's largely gonna be due to

00:06:01.910 --> 00:06:03.670
investment in to high tech sectors,

00:06:03.670 --> 00:06:06.250
that can eventually
drive up the labor costs.

00:06:06.250 --> 00:06:08.180
- [Narrator] But Chen says,
dealing with that issue

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:10.380
is far more predictable than figuring out

00:06:10.380 --> 00:06:13.700
what the World's Superpowers
decide to do with Taiwan.

00:06:13.700 --> 00:06:14.600
- From our perspective,

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:16.580
we really would like
to see steady policies.

00:06:16.580 --> 00:06:20.230
No major policy changes, not
for China, not for the U.S.

00:06:20.230 --> 00:06:21.260
and not for Taiwan.

00:06:21.260 --> 00:06:25.319
But, I think there's only so
much that we can do about that.

00:06:25.319 --> 00:06:27.986
(ancient music)

